.TH POLO 1 "November 2026" "Polo @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
polo \- Wayland compositor for the MATE desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polo
.RB [ \-\-session ]
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B polo
is a Wayland compositor and window manager for MATE.
It is built on a private copy of libweston, loads MATE's window manager
settings (the
.B org.mate.Marco.*
keys) and runs X11 programs through its own XWayland window manager.
.PP
Normally it is started by the display manager as the
.B MATE (Polo)
session, with
.BR \-\-session ;
see
.BR polo\-session (7).
Without
.BR \-\-session
it starts only the compositor, for testing.
Inside a Wayland session it opens a window that is the screen
.RB ( \-\-backend=wayland );
on a text console it drives the screens itself
.RB ( \-\-backend=drm ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-session
Run as the MATE session: provide
.BR org.gnome.SessionManager ,
start the session's programs, start XWayland at once and use the Polo dconf
profile.
It refuses to start if another session manager is running.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend= NAME
.BR drm ,
.B wayland
or
.BR headless .
The default is
.B wayland
inside a Wayland session and otherwise
.BR drm .
.TP
.BI \-\-renderer= NAME
.BR auto ,
.B gl
or
.BR pixman .
Some effects need
.BR gl .
.TP
.BI \-\-xwayland= MODE
.BR off ,
.B lazy
(start XWayland when the first X11 client connects) or
.BR eager .
The default is
.BR lazy ;
a session uses
.BR eager .
.TP
.BI \-\-width= PIXELS ", " \-\-height= PIXELS
Size of nested or headless outputs.
.TP
.BI \-\-scale= N
Scale of nested or headless outputs.
.TP
.BI \-\-scales= LIST
Scale of each nested or headless output, as
.BR 1,2 .
.TP
.BI \-\-outputs= N
Number of nested or headless outputs.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Open the nested output fullscreen.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket= NAME
Name of the Wayland socket.
The default is the first free
.BR wayland\-N .
.TP
.BI \-\-exec= COMMAND
Run
.I COMMAND
as a client once Polo has started.
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-log= FILE
Write the log to
.I FILE
instead of standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-debug\-scopes= A,B
Also print the debug messages of these log scopes (for example
.BR polo,drm\-backend ).
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Log frame, input and effect timings every 10 seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-debug\-kill
Let Ctrl+Alt+Backspace end Polo at once.
Only builds made for development
.RB ( \-Ddebug\-kill=true )
act on it; in other builds the option is accepted and does nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POLO_XWAYLAND
Chooses the XWayland mode like
.BR \-\-xwayland .
.TP
.B POLO_WATCHDOG_SECONDS
With the
.B drm
backend a watchdog logs a main loop that stops responding for over a second,
with where it is stuck.
Set this to a number of seconds to make Polo abort, and so leave a core dump,
when the main loop is stuck that long; the default is not to abort, and
.B 0
only logs.
Polo does not abort while the system is short of memory or the main loop is
waiting in the kernel, for the GPU for instance.
.TP
.B POLO_STATS_INTERVAL_MS
Turns on the timing summaries of
.B \-\-stats
and sets their interval.
.TP
.B POLO_SHELL_UI
Path of the helper that draws the Alt+Tab switcher, window menus, dialogs and
on-screen displays instead of
.IR polo\-shell\-ui .
Empty means none.
.TP
.B POLO_DATA_DIR
Directory to use instead of
.I /usr/share/polo
(it holds the portal configuration).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/polo\-shell\-ui
The helper for the switcher, window menus, dialogs and on-screen displays.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/polo\-share\-chooser
The screen sharing chooser.
.TP
.I /usr/lib64/polo/
Polo's private libweston and its modules; nothing else uses them.
.TP
.I /usr/share/glib\-2.0/schemas/org.mate.polo.gschema.xml
Polo's own settings:
.BR org.mate.polo.general ,
.BR org.mate.polo.session ,
.BR org.mate.polo.effects
and
.BR org.mate.polo.keybindings .
.TP
.I ~/.config/mate/polo/monitors.xml
The saved screen layout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
after a normal end of the session or
.BR \-\-version ,
non-zero if Polo could not start.
If Polo dies of a signal it first writes the signal, a backtrace and the end
of its log to its log, then dies of the same signal so that the system keeps a
core dump
.RB ( coredumpctl\ list\ polo ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR polo\-session (7)
